; lowering-aggregate corpus: a form's `:lowering :produces` names a head
; qualified to the `storage` plugin, which is never loaded. The namespace
; is spelled explicitly, so `Schema.validateLowering` reports the dangling
; edge as `lowering_target_plugin_absent` (not the generic `unknown_form`
; a bare or same-plugin miss gets) — an aggregate-time check, before any
; hook runs. The `(plain)` data form is non-lowering, so the runtime
; lowering pass stays a no-op and only the aggregate diagnostic surfaces.
(plugin :name pngine :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name pass :open true
    :lowering (lowering :hook pngine/pass-v1 :produces [storage/table-row]))
  (form :name plain :open true))

(plain)
